<title>USA: IBM CFO exit not a negative - SoundView.</title>
<headline>IBM CFO exit not a negative - SoundView.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The departure of International Business Machines Corp Chief Financial Officer G. Richard Thoman to Xerox Corp is not a negative to IBM, said Gary Helmig, a SoundView Financial analyst.</p>
<p>&quot;Jerry York was really the heads-down, take-no-prisoners, get-rid-of-costs-and-expenses kind of guy,&quot; Helmig said, referring to IBM's CFO before Thoman took over in 1995.</p>
<p>&quot;Thoman has been executing on this, but the hard stuff, a lot of it was done.  I just don't see this as being a negative for IBM.&quot;  Helmig said any decline in IBM's shares Thursday as a result of the news is a buying opportunity.</p>
</text>
